<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of text, set as verse in italic. Below the poem: the signed initials "I. I. B." right-aligned, then a printer's ornament. No margin notes. Running head at top centre, page number at top right.</layout>
  <page_number>63</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Victor splendidus obteris,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Et tristi patriam funere liberas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Heu!mens cæca cupidine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Quum regni rapitur, quo ruit impetu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Præceps per vetitum nefas?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Nullum turpe putat flagitium, aut scelus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Leges iuraque[?] negligit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Cælesti arbitrio cuncta negans regi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Nullos illa deos, neque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Plectendis metuit Tartara sontibus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Fertur filia mortuum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Conculcasse ferox Tullia Seruium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Bigis, dum properat patris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Regem cæde sui cernere coniugem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Regno fraudibus impiis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Dauidem pepulit filius Absalom.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Quem mox dextera Numinis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Feriens ætherei perdidit exitu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Tristi, qui manet improbos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Conatus meritum supplicium ferens.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">I. I. B.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Ornament (printer's flower piece) below the signature, not transcribed. Faint mirrored text on the right and a faint word at lower left are show-through from the other side and were left out. "iuraque" has a doubtful accent over the a, marked [?]. The printed word "Dauidem" and the spellings are as printed.</notes>
</page>
